From 06dfbcaafab3e6bc98fd2cbed85c9ee884bbfd2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:58:21 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] docs(guide): add "Your first 4-axis part" (3+1 indexed,
 770MX + microARC 4)

A start-to-finish walkthrough of indexed 3+1 work on the Tormach 770MX
with the microARC 4: a round bar with a flat on each of four faces
(A-90, A0, A90, A180) and a cross slot, as five typed Slot operations
that each carry their own Tilted plane index.

- site/content/guide/getting-started/first-4axis-part.md: the page,
  linked from the Getting started index, first-run.md and the
  Multi-axis index.
- examples/first-4axis-part.camproj, .nc and models/first-4axis-part.obj
  (with its generator): the companion project, the program it posts and
  the model.
- crates/app/tests/first_4axis_part.rs builds the project through the
  app's commands and holds the program to the post.
- site/tests/test_first_4axis_part.py holds the page to the UI sources,
  the project and the posted program.

The continuous 4-axis walkthrough is not part of this change: tormach.cps
refuses an A that changes inside an operation, and #796 is open.

Refs #1904

