From e955c9dfed47e7c2d1ce0a73ffd335fa72c04a99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:47:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(multiaxis): refuse out-of-range 3+2 tilt by name and
 keep A0 B180 plane X on machine X

- Add Tilt::refusal and wire it into OpParams::named_refusal and
  feedback::apply_hint so an out-of-range Tool axis A or B names the
  field, states the canonical -90..90 / -180..180 bounds, and gives the
  A 0 B 180 pose for the face opposite the top.
- Zero axis components below 1e-12 in TiltedFrame::new before picking the
  tie-breaking seed axis so sin(180 deg) float dust no longer swaps X
  and Y on the A 0 B 180 face.
- Stacked on #2135: update first-4axis-part.md, first_4axis_part.rs, and
  examples/first-4axis-part.camproj so Flat A180 uses the same along-X
  ends as the other three flats.
- Pin with unit, app/MCP, and UI Apply-hint tests, and record the
  decision in docs/decisions/2133-tilt-a180-refusal-basis.md.

Fixes #2133
